{"builder":"Goal: one pull request for issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 (padLeft for invoice numbers) that meets every one of these acceptance lines:\n1. index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\n2. padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\n3. README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\n4. npm test passes\n\nContext: this is an ES module package (\"type\": \"module\"). index.js currently exports capitalize, slugify and truncate. README.md has `## capitalize(s)` and `## truncate(s, n)` sections but NO section for slugify, so line 3 is already unmet before you add padLeft. Tests live in test/strutil.test.js and run with `npm test` (node --test).\n\nSteps:\n1. In index.js add `export function padLeft(s, width, fill = ' ')` with a short doc comment in the same style as the others. It must return s padded on the left with fill until it is width characters long (e.g. padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042', padLeft('42', 5) === '   42'), and must return s unchanged when s.length >= width (e.g. padLeft('123456', 5, '0') === '123456'). String.prototype.padStart is fine.\n2. In README.md add a `## padLeft(s, width, fill)` section describing it, including the default space fill and the unchanged-when-long-enough behaviour. Also add the missing `## slugify(s)` section (lower case, words joined by dashes, as in index.js). Keep the heading form `## name(args)` so every exported function has its own section. Do not remove existing sections.\n3. In test/strutil.test.js add a padLeft test covering: zero padding ('42', 5, '0' -> '00042'), default space fill, s exactly width long, and s longer than width. Do not weaken or delete existing tests.\n4. Run `npm test` and confirm all tests pass (0 failures).\n5. Run this to confirm every exported function has a README section; it must print ALL PRESENT and list padLeft among the exports:\n   node --input-type=module -e 'import * as m from \"./index.js\"; import fs from \"node:fs\"; const r = fs.readFileSync(\"README.md\", \"utf8\"); const fns = Object.keys(m).filter((k) => typeof m[k] === \"function\"); const miss = fns.filter((k) => !new RegExp(\"^#{1,6}\\\\s+`?\" + k + \"\\\\b\", \"m\").test(r)); console.log(\"exports: \" + fns.join(\",\")); console.log(miss.length ? \"MISSING: \" + miss.join(\",\") : \"ALL PRESENT\");'\n6. Commit index.js, README.md and the test file, and open the pull request referencing issue #7.","verifier":"Verify the pull request for https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 at its head commit. Run every command from the repository root. There is one check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun:\n  node --input-type=module -e 'import { padLeft } from \"./index.js\"; const c = [[padLeft(\"42\", 5, \"0\"), \"00042\"], [padLeft(\"42\", 5), \"   42\"], [padLeft(\"ab\", 4, \"*\"), \"**ab\"], [padLeft(\"x\", 1, \"0\"), \"x\"], [padLeft(\"\", 3, \"0\"), \"000\"]]; let ok = true; for (const [got, want] of c) { const pass = got === want; ok = ok && pass; console.log(JSON.stringify(got), pass ? \"==\" : \"!=\", JSON.stringify(want)); } console.log(ok ? \"ALL OK\" : \"MISMATCH\");'\nPASS: the import succeeds and the last line is ALL OK (left padding with the given fill, a space when fill is omitted, to exactly width characters).\nFAIL: an import error (padLeft not exported), any thrown error, or MISMATCH.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun:\n  node --input-type=module -e 'import { padLeft } from \"./index.js\"; const c = [[\"00042\", 5, \"0\"], [\"123456\", 5, \"0\"], [\"hello\", 3], [\"abc\", 0, \"*\"]]; let ok = true; for (const [s, w, f] of c) { const got = padLeft(s, w, f); const pass = got === s; ok = ok && pass; console.log(JSON.stringify([s, w, f]), \"->\", JSON.stringify(got), pass ? \"unchanged\" : \"CHANGED\"); } console.log(ok ? \"ALL OK\" : \"MISMATCH\");'\nPASS: every line says unchanged and the last line is ALL OK.\nFAIL: any CHANGED line, MISMATCH, or an error.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun:\n  node --input-type=module -e 'import * as m from \"./index.js\"; import fs from \"node:fs\"; const r = fs.readFileSync(\"README.md\", \"utf8\"); const fns = Object.keys(m).filter((k) => typeof m[k] === \"function\"); const miss = fns.filter((k) => !new RegExp(\"^#{1,6}\\\\s+`?\" + k + \"\\\\b\", \"m\").test(r)); console.log(\"exports: \" + fns.join(\",\")); console.log(miss.length ? \"MISSING: \" + miss.join(\",\") : \"ALL PRESENT\");'\nThen open README.md and confirm each matched heading starts a section that actually describes that function.\nPASS: the script prints ALL PRESENT, and every exported function (including slugify, which had no section before this change, and padLeft) has its own heading with a description beneath it.\nFAIL: the script prints MISSING for any name, or some function's heading has no describing content.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"npm test passes\"\nRun:\n  npm test\nPASS: exit code 0 and the summary shows fail 0.\nFAIL: non-zero exit code or any failing test.\n\nAdvisory (not part of any PASS/FAIL):\n- Note whether test/strutil.test.js gained padLeft tests and whether existing tests were left intact.\n- Note behaviour with a multi-character fill or non-string input, if you look, but do not fail on it."}